{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** Given an array `nums`, count its **inversions**: pairs of indexes `i < j` with `nums[i] > nums[j]`. The count measures how far the array is from sorted — 0 for a sorted array, n(n − 1)/2 for a reversed one."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/2932f6d0-1092-4175-ad57-b4fcae8ee05d.svg",
      "alt": "Merging the sorted halves 2, 4 and 1, 3, 5. When 1 is taken from the right half, the left half still holds 2 and 4, both bigger than 1 and both earlier in the array: 2 inversions at once. When 3 is taken, 4 is still waiting: 1 more.",
      "width": 737,
      "height": 367,
      "scene": {
